<p>Of climb batch 29b&rsquo;s changes, five change or add rules: the change to change 40, under which a numeral&rsquo;s type has its four numbers as static arguments and a program&rsquo;s own number type takes a numeral through a coercion generic over them, in place of a coercion that reads getters; the change to change 41, which gives the rule&rsquo;s answer for <code>=</code> between a number and a numeral, and the form to write; the change to change 70, under which a folded constant reaches a program&rsquo;s own type only through a coercion from its default type; the change to change 75, under which a numeral type&rsquo;s numbers, used as values, are <code>ZZ</code> values; and change 86, under which the prelude&rsquo;s numerals are the one exception to the rule that adds nothing to the prelude. The others, changes 84 and 85 and the changes to changes 42, 68 and 78, state facts that the batch changed, name departures and traps that it found, or cut words that state no rule.</p>
